{
  "assessment": "The source provides the asymptotic MSD scaling exponent gamma(alpha) for the RILW model, with alpha=2 giving gamma=1 and alpha=4 giving gamma=1.5. The final-decade fitting scope (t_ref=1e7, t_max=1e8) is supported by the simulation description and figure caption. The normalized MSD ratio M(r)=r^gamma is a derived quantity consistent with the power-law scaling. The extraction is complete and case_authoring_ready is true.",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Soma Shiraki, Tunable Anomalous Diffusion in Subrecoil-Laser-Cooled Atoms, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/9pb2-v6zs",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/9pb2-v6zs",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2503.15027v1"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper analyzes anomalous diffusion in subrecoil-laser-cooled atoms using the rate-induced Levy walk (RILW) and inhomogeneous random walk (IRW) models, with a velocity-dependent fluorescence rate R(v) proportional to |v|^alpha. It derives the asymptotic MSD scaling exponent gamma(alpha) and validates it numerically. The selected cluster focuses on the normalized MSD scaling ratio M(r)=MSD(t)/MSD(t_ref)=r^gamma for alpha=2 and alpha=4, using the final-decade fitting scope.",
